.\" Manual page for gans(1). Rendered into /usr/share/man/man1/gans.1.gz by
.\" packaging/build-deb.sh. Keep the option/command list in step with gans/cli.py.
.TH GANS 1 "2026-09-04" "Gans" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gans \- Ente Auth two-factor codes, one keystroke away (tray agent)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gans
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B gans
.RB { \-\-version | \-\-help }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gans
is a tray-resident client for Ente Auth, the open-source two-factor
authenticator. It signs in to your Ente account, syncs your end-to-end
encrypted codes, and keeps them one keystroke away: the tray menu lists every
entry with its live code (click to copy), and the global hotkey (Ctrl+Alt+Space
by default) opens Quick Search, a search field that types the selected code
into the previous field on X11, or copies it on Wayland.
.PP
Only one instance runs per session. Running
.B gans
again while it is running forwards the command to the running instance over
D-Bus, so a desktop keyboard shortcut can simply run
.BR "gans toggle" .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I (none)
Start the tray agent, or open Quick Search if it is already running.
.TP
.B toggle
Show or hide Quick Search in the running instance. This is the command to bind
to a keyboard shortcut when Gans cannot register the hotkey itself.
.TP
.B search
Show Quick Search.
.TP
.B settings
Open the Settings window.
.TP
.B quit
Quit the running instance.
.TP
.BI ente-cli:// URL
The passkey redirect from the browser during sign-in. The desktop file registers
.B gans
as the handler for the
.B ente-cli
URL scheme so this is normally invoked by the browser, not by hand.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GANS_GDK_BACKEND
GDK backend to run on. Gans defaults to X11 (XWayland in a Wayland session)
for tray clipboard ownership and popup placement. Set this to
.B wayland
to use native Wayland. All Wayland sessions use clipboard delivery;
XWayland cannot reliably identify the focused native window.
.TP
.B GANS_DEBUG
When set to a non-empty value, enables debug logging on standard error. Logs
never contain secrets, tokens, or codes.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/gans/preferences.json
Preferences (hotkey, delivery mode, clipboard clearing, app lock, usage
statistics). Defaults to
.IR ~/.config/gans/preferences.json .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/gans/entities.json
Cache of the account's entries exactly as Ente stores them: still encrypted,
useless without the key held in the keyring. Defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share/gans/entities.json .
.TP
.I ~/.config/autostart/ch.lkmc.Gans.desktop
Present when "Launch at login" is enabled in Settings.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/ch.lkmc.gans.policy
The polkit action behind the optional app lock (auth_self: the desktop asks for
your own password).
.PP
The session token and the authenticator key are stored in the Secret Service
(GNOME Keyring, KWallet, or KeePassXC) under the
.B gans
application attribute. Without a Secret Service the session is kept in memory
only and you sign in again after a restart; nothing secret is ever written to
disk in plaintext.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
Unknown command or option.
.SH SEE ALSO
.UR https://github.com/L-K-M/Gans
Project page and Linux notes
.UE
.br
.UR https://ente.io/auth/
Ente Auth
.UE
